                     {
                         "t":  "1. Hero \u0026 Intro ",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Laser Hair Removal",
                         "b":  true
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Waxing every few weeks, threading the upper lip, shaving before every trip. For most of us it started in our teens and never really stopped. Add the ingrown hairs, the rashes and the dark patches that years of waxing can leave, and it\u0027s easy to see why so many people start looking into laser hair removal in Delhi.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Lasers work differently. Instead of pulling hair out, it weakens the root so it grows back less, and what does grow back is usually finer and lighter. It takes a course of sessions, not one visit, but most people end up with far less hair to deal with and a lot more free time. The treatment is suitable for both men and women, and for almost any area of the body.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Available at Dadu Medical Centre Vasant Vihar (South Delhi) \u0026 Rajouri Garden (West Delhi), under Dr. Nivedita Dadu.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "h2",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "2. How Laser Hair Removal Works",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "The laser looks for the pigment inside the hair follicle. When it finds it, the light turns into heat and damages the follicle enough that it struggles to produce hair again.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "There\u0027s a reason it takes several sessions. Hair grows in cycles, and the laser only works on follicles that are in their active growth phase at the time. Others are resting and will come up later, so sessions are spaced out to catch each new round. With every visit, a few more follicles stop working and the hair gets noticeably thinner.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "h2",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "3. Lasers We Use",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Not every laser suits every skin and hair type, which is why the clinic has more than one. Your specialist chooses after looking at your skin tone, hair colour and thickness, and the area being treated.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Soprano ICE:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " a diode laser with built-in cooling, used across all skin tones and for both coarse and fine hair",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Diode laser (810nm):",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " suited to medium to dark skin with coarse, dark hair",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Alexandrite laser (755nm):",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " better for fair to medium skin with fine to medium hair",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Titanium Soprano:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " a multi-wavelength system that can be used on all skin and hair types",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Older hair removal lasers carried a real risk of burns or pigment changes on darker skin. Today\u0027s diode and Soprano systems are considered safe for most Indian skin types, provided they\u0027re used by experienced professionals.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "h2",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "4. Areas That Can Be Treated",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Almost anywhere with unwanted hair. For women, the face, upper lip, chin and sideburns are common requests, along with underarms, arms, legs, bikini line and stomach. Men often book the back, chest and stomach, and many come in for beard shaping to keep the neck and cheek lines clean.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
