    {
        "k":  "h2",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "6. Ideal Candidates",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Anyone tired of the waxing and shaving routine, whether for the face or the body. Women dealing with facial hair, men who want a less hairy back or chest, and people who get ingrown hairs or irritation from waxing all tend to benefit. It also suits brides and grooms, though it\u0027s best to start early since the course runs over several months.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Things to know:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " Laser works by targeting pigment, so very light, grey or blonde hair may not respond well. Hormonal conditions can also make new hair grow over time, which is why some people need maintenance. Your doctor will check your skin, hair and medical history at the consultation before recommending a laser. ",
                         "b":  false
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  "(The live page doesn\u0027t list contraindications or the grey/blonde hair limitation: please have Dr. Nivedita Dadu confirm these points, and any other precautions such as pregnancy, recent tanning or photosensitising medicines, before publishing.)",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
